.TH THUNDERBIRD-TRAY 1 "October 2026" "thunderbird-tray" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
thunderbird-tray \- Thunderbird tray companion for Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B thunderbird-tray
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B thunderbird-tray doctor
.br
.B thunderbird-tray settings
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B thunderbird-tray
receives aggregate Inbox unread state from a Thunderbird 156 or newer
Manifest V3 extension through Native Messaging and exposes a Linux
StatusNotifierItem tray icon and menu.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B doctor
Print a privacy-preserving diagnostic report.
.TP
.B settings
Open the graphical settings window.
.TP
.BR --config " " PATH
Use a specific configuration file.
.TP
.BR --window-backend " " BACKEND
Select auto, kde-wayland, x11, or unsupported window control.
.TP
.BR --log-level " " LEVEL
Select trace, debug, info, warn, or error logging.
.TP
.B --help
Show command-line help.
.TP
.B --version
Show the application version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/thunderbird-tray/config.toml
Default per-user configuration file.
.TP
.I /opt/thunderbird-tray/share/thunderbird-tray/thunderbird-tray.xpi
Thunderbird extension installed separately through Add-ons Manager.
.SH SEE ALSO
The packaged README files in
.IR /opt/thunderbird-tray/ .
